//	more](https://resend.com/docs/dashboard/emails/idempotency-keys)
//	cc: CC recipient email address. For multiple addresses, send as an array of
//	strings. Counts toward the 50-recipient limit. Each address is
//	`email@example.com` or `Name <email@example.com>`. An address that is not
//	valid returns a 422.
//	bcc: BCC recipient email address. For multiple addresses, send as an array
//	of strings. Counts toward the 50-recipient limit. Each address is
//	`email@example.com` or `Name <email@example.com>`. An address that is not
//	valid returns a 422.
//	html: An HTML note sent above the quoted original.
//	text: A plain-text note sent above the quoted original.
//	subject: The subject of the forward. Cannot be only whitespace or contain a
//	line break. When omitted, the thread subject is used, prefixed with `Fwd:`
//	if it does not already start with it.
